                          --------------------
                          Muddles changes file
                          --------------------

Version 4.50 - 30 Apr 95
------------------------

* Now supports the SCREEN0-SCREEN7 keywords in the Metro.cfg file for
re-mapping screen colours.

Version 4.40 - 27 Jan 95
------------------------

* End-of-File check routine re-written.  Now hundreds of times faster.
Also will ask you if you want to "repair" a file which fails the EOF
check on the spot.  Please:  ONLY REPAIR THE FILE IF IT'S A TEXTFILE!

Repairing a binary file will result in a Linefeed character appended to
the end of it, probably NOT a good idea!  (But easy to remove if you do
do it accidentally).

* Filenotes will be used as the default description in the "Quick Add"
and "Add from Dir" functions.  If there is no filenote on the file, the
default "Added by Muddles" or the one you specify in the "Quick Add"
function.  However, if there is a filenote, it will be used as the
default description instead.  This will make it much easier to transfer
platforms where the description might already be attached to the file
via a filenote, and using the "Quick Add" function will make them
available to OzMetro completely automatically.

If you want the opportunity to review each file one at a time, use the
"Add from Dir" function, and then you can edit the filenote before
adding the file to the file list.

Beware of TrapDoor-added filenote (eg:  "From 3:622/422.0; Secure NL;
Trx 2f0f32fe/2f0f3259; Time d18a1254;").  These might get included at
some point.  Using the "Add From Dir" menu item will help to avert this
(although take a lot longer to add the files).

Also, the filenote has to be truncated to 76 characters to fit into the
filelist structure.  So you might lose up to the final three characters
of an existing description.  Sorry!

